## 1. Why this document exists

DESIGN is architecture narrative; SPEC is fuller normative detail; RFCs are numbered evolutionary proposals (e.g. 0001 capabilities, 0002 contracts).

## 2. Problem statement

Language change without process becomes chat-driven. RFCs provide reviewable evolution under DESIGN/SPEC.

## 3. Related work (university + commercial)

- IETF RFC process.
- Rust RFCs / Python PEPs.
- ADRs for smaller decisions. https://adr.github.io/

## 4. Rationale for openOODA

DESIGN north star; SPEC normative; RFC proposed change; PM implementation; residual alpha honesty.

## 5. Limits and failure modes

RFCs without implementation become fiction. Dual DESIGN paths can drift. Not every residual needs an RFC.

## 6. Alternatives considered

Wiki-only, issue-tracker-only, single mega-README, or oral tradition — all fail multi-agent continuity or honesty. Prefer git-versioned markdown with clear roles.

## 7. Reality (honesty)

RFCs 0001/0002 exist; process maturity partial.

## 8. Open questions

1. Require RFC for DESIGN leaf → done?
2. Single canonical DESIGN path?

## 9. Acceptance criteria

- [ ] New language features cite RFC or residual.
- [ ] SPEC does not contradict PM honesty.

## 10. References

1. openOODA/openOODA/rfcs/
2. https://adr.github.io/

